    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105162" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῐ-πόθητος</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρί̆-ᾱτος</span></b>  (s. v. l.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>thrice</i> (i. e. <i>much</i>) <i>longed for,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ τριπόθατε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Bion
					1.58
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Mosch.
				3.51
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶαρ τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Bion
					<u>Fr.</u>
					15.15
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. Ἄδωνις</span> Hymn. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Hippol.
				<u>Haer.</u>
				5.9
			</span></i>; also in late Prose, as <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Hist.Conscr.</u>
				31
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
